            <div type="general">
               <p xml:space="preserve">El Kef is the capital of its eponymous Tunisian governorate. It is located in the northwestern part of the country in the Tunisian-Algerian border region. Though beyond Tunisia’s touristic regions, the small town provides interesting insights into Tunisia’s cultural and historical heritage. </p>
               <p>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-roman-bath.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic018"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-roman-bath.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic018"/>
                     <head>Roman bath</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-Franzi-bath.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic019"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-Franzi-bath.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic019"/>
                     <head>Researcher Franzi in front the Roman baths ruins</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-flowers.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic020"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-flowers.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic020"/>
                     <head>Flowers planted within the area of the Roman baths</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-baths-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic021"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-baths-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic021"/>
                     <head>Roman bath</head>
                  </figure>
               </p>
               <p xml:space="preserve">Ruins of a Roman bath (<hi xml:lang="aeb" rendition="#i">ḥammām</hi>) evoke the country’s antique past, while the Kasbah (<hi xml:lang="aeb" rendition="#i">qaṣba</hi>), a fort with a view over the whole town, goes back to the time of Ottoman rule. </p>
               <p>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-kasba.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic022"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-kasba.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic022"/>
                     <head>Inside the Kasbah: beautiful stairs</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-kasba-guns.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic023"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-kasba-guns.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic023"/>
                     <head>Guns of the Kasbah</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-kasba-entrance.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic024"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-kasba-entrance.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic024"/>
                     <head>Entrance of the Kasbah</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-kasba-view.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic025"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-kasba-view.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic025"/>
                     <head>View of the city from the the Kasbah</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-kasba-guns-view.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic026"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-kasba-guns-view.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic026"/>
                     <head>Guns of and view from the Kasbah</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-kasba-night.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic027"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-kasba-night.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic027"/>
                     <head>The Kasbah Illuminated at Night</head>
                  </figure>
               </p>
               <p xml:space="preserve">An old synagogue in the centre of El Kef as well as a Jewish and a Christian cemetery are indicators of the former times’ religious diversity.</p>
               <p>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-synagogue-road.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic028"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-synagogue-road.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic028"/>
                     <head>On the way to the Synagogue de la Ghriba</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-synagogue-entrance.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic029"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-synagogue-entrance.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic029"/>
                     <head>Entrance of the Synagogue de la Ghriba</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-synagogue-yard.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic030"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-synagogue-yard.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic030"/>
                     <head>Yard with Ruins of the Synagogue de la Ghriba</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-synagogue-inside.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic031"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-synagogue-inside.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic031"/>
                     <head>Inside the Synagogue de la Ghriba</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-cemeteries.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic032"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-cemeteries.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic032"/>
                     <head>Jewish and Christian cemeteries</head>
                  </figure>
               </p>
               <p xml:space="preserve">In addition to the mosque, the mausoleum of the local saint Sidi Bou Makhlouf (Sīdi Bū Maxlūf) is one of the holy places people visit to the present.</p>
               <p>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-makhlouf-sign.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic033"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-makhlouf-sign.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic033"/>
                     <head>Tombs of Bou Makhlouf </head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-makhlouf-door.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic034"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-makhlouf-door.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic034"/>
                     <head>Tombs of Bou Makhlouf</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-makhlouf-tomb.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic035"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-makhlouf-tomb.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic035"/>
                     <head>Tombs of Bou Makhlouf </head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-makhlouf-tomb-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic036"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-makhlouf-tomb-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic036"/>
                     <head>Tombs of Bou Makhlouf</head>
                  </figure>
               </p>
               <p xml:space="preserve">While historical traces are omnipresent, professional graffiti arts embellish roads, paths and public places showing the modern side of El Kef. </p>
               <p rendition="#slideshow">
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-makhlouf.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic037"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-makhlouf.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic037"/>
                     <head>Graffiti of Bou Makhlouf</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-bird.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic038"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-bird.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic038"/>
                     <head>Graffiti of a dove by Wiss</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic039"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic039"/>
                     <head>Graffiti calligraphy I</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic040"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic040"/>
                     <head>Graffiti calligraphy II</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy-3.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic041"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy-3.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic041"/>
                     <head>Graffiti calligraphy III</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-old-man.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic042"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-old-man.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic042"/>
                     <head>Graffiti of an old man</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-berber.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic043"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-berber.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic043"/>
                     <head>Graffiti of an Berber woman</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy-4.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic044"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-calligraphy-4.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic044"/>
                     <head>Kefian proverb</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-park.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic045"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-park.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic045"/>
                     <head>Graffiti on a park entrance</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-basketball.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic046"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-basketball.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic046"/>
                     <head>Graffiti of old men playing basketball</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-vase.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic047"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-vase.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic047"/>
                     <head>Ornated vase</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure rendition="#small">
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-wiss.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic048"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-wiss.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic048"/>
                     <head>Artist Wiss in front of his graffiti of an eye</head>
                  </figure>
               </p>
               <p xml:space="preserve">Some Kefian artists even integrate the town’s past into their work, using El Kef’s former Latin name Sicca Veneria as a graffiti motif. </p>
               <p rendition="#full-width">
                  <figure>
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-1.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic049"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-1.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic049"/>
                     <head>Graffiti SICCA</head>
                  </figure>
                  <figure>
                     <link target="Kef-graffiti-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic050"/>
                     <graphic url="Kef-graffiti-2.jpg" decls="#profile_kef_01_graphic050"/>
                     <head>Graffiti VENERIA</head>
                  </figure>
               </p>
